[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Alekhine Defence"]
[Variation "Alekhine Defence: Modern Variation"]
[ECO "B04"]
[Character "positional,solid"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "space,develop-fast"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "1...Nf6"]
[Start "1. e4"]

1... Nf6 2. e5 { Attacks the knight at once. It must move, so White gains a tempo (a free move) and space. } 2... Nd5 3. d4 { Builds a big centre while the knight is stuck out on d5. Black will try to attack these pawns later. } 3... d6 ( 3... g6 4. c4 { Chases the knight from d5 with a pawn before it can settle there. } 4... Nb6 5. Nc3 { Develops and gets ready for c5, which would hit the knight on b6 with nowhere safe to go. } 5... Bg7 6. c5 { Attacks the knight, which has no good square: after ...d5 cxb6 White wins a piece. } ) 4. Nf3 { Develops and defends e5, so that ...dxe5 can be answered with Nxe5. } 4... Bg4 ( 4... dxe5 5. Nxe5 { Wins the pawn back with a knight that now sits in the centre. } ) 5. Be2 { Defends the knight on f3, which the bishop pins against the queen, and prepares to castle. } 5... e6 6. O-O { Castles early: the king is safe and the rook joins in once the centre opens. } 6... Be7 7. h3 { Asks the bishop what it wants. After ...Bh5 the c4 push is coming; after ...Bxf3 White gets the two bishops. } 7... Bh5 8. c4 { Chases the knight from d5 with a pawn. The knight has to give up its good square. } 8... Nb6 9. Nc3 { Plan: develop the rest (Be3, Qd2 or Rc1) and keep e5 protected. If Black takes on e5, recapture and keep the extra space; trading pieces suits the side with more room. } *
